anding the right-hand side:\n\n\\[ (a + b)c^{2} = a^{4} + 2a^{2}b^{2} + b^{4} \\]\n\n8. Thus, we have:\n\n\\[ a^4 + 2a^2b^2 + b^4 \\leq a^4 + a^3b + ab^3 + b^4 \\]\n\n9. By the AM-GM inequality,\n\n\\[ 2a^2b^2 \\leq a^3b + ab^3 \\]\n\n10. Therefore, the inequality holds. This completes the first solution proof.\n\n**Second Solution:**\n\n1. Assume \\( a \\leq b \\).\n\n2. We need to prove \\( c^{2} - (a + b)c + ab \\leq 0 \\).\n\n3. Consider the quadratic equation relative to \\( c \\):\n\n\\[ c^{2} - (a + b)c + ab \\]\n\nThis quadratic will have roots when the discriminant (\\( \\Delta \\)) is non-negative.\n\n4. Calculate the discriminant:\n\n\\[ \\Delta = (a + b)^{2} - 4ab = a^{2} + 2ab + b^{2} - 4ab = a^{2} - 2ab + b^{2} = (a - b)^{2} \\]\n\n5. Since \\( (a - b)^{2} \\geq 0 \\), the discriminant is non-negative, and the quadratic has real roots. The quadratic expression is non-positive between its roots.\n\n6. Thus, \\( c \\) lies between its roots \\( a \\) and \\( b \\). Specifically, \n\n\\[ a \\leq c \\leq b \\]\n\n7. Verifying these inequalities,\n\n\\[ c^{2} = a^{2} + b^{2} - ab \\leq b^{2} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad c^{2} = a^{2} + b^{2} - ab \\geq a^{2} \\]\n\n8. From \\( c^{2} = b^{2} + a(a - b) \\leq b^{2} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad c^{2} = a^{2} + b(b - a) \\geq a^{2} \\),\n\nSince both conditions hold, thus, we have:\n\n\\[ c^{2}+ab \\leq ac+bc \\]\n\nThis completes the proof for the second solution.\n\nThus, indeed: \n\n\\[ \\boxed{c^2 + ab \\leq ac + bc} \\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "Carpet merchant Alibaba has a rectangular carpet of unknown dimensions. Unfortunately, his measuring tape is broken, and he has no other measuring tools. However, he discovered that when the carpet is laid flat in either of his two shops, each corner of the carpet exactly meets different walls of the shop. He knows that the length and width of the carpet are both integers in feet. The two shops ha