 family's monthly income to save an additional 5% of this amount while maintaining their other expenses? What will be the amount of savings in this case after 10 months?\"\n\nSo the first part is the required income. The second part is the amount of savings in this case. If \"in this case\" refers to the scenario where they save an additional 5%, then the savings would be the 5% each month. Alternatively, if \"savings\" refers to all their savings (existing and additional), then it's 5,000 + 5% of income. But since the problem says \"save an additional 5%\", it's likely that the 5% is the extra saving, so the total savings would include both the original 5,000 and the new 5% (3,250). But the problem is not explicit. Let me check the exact wording.\n\nThe problem states they want to \"save an additional 5% of this amount\". The \"additional\" implies on top of whatever they were saving before. But in their current expenses, they already have 5,000 RUB as savings. So if they want to save an additional 5%, that would mean the total savings would be 5,000 + 5% of income. However, when calculating the required income, we considered that their total expenses (including the 5,000) plus the additional 5% must equal income. Wait, no. Let me think again.\n\nIf their current expenses are 61,750 RUB, which includes the 5,000 savings, then their current income must be at least 61,750 RUB to break even. If they want to save an additional 5% of their income, then their income needs to be such that:\n\nIncome = Current Expenses + Additional Savings\n\nWhere Additional Savings = 5% of Income.\n\nTherefore:\n\nX = 61,750 + 0.05X\n\nX - 0.05X = 61,750\n\n0.95X = 61,750\n\nX = 61,750 / 0.95 = 65,000 RUB.\n\nSo the monthly income should be 65,000 RUB. Then, the additional savings each month is 5% of 65,000 = 3,250 RUB. Therefore, after 10 months, the total additional savings would be 3,250 *10 = 32,500 RUB. However, if the question is asking for the total savings (including the original