ertex of the upper base (e.g., \\(C'\\)).\n\n2. **Dihedral Angle Calculation**:\n   - The dihedral angle between the cross-section plane and the lower base is \\(45^\\circ\\).\n   - Using the normal vectors of the planes, we find the relationship between \\(a\\) and \\(h\\):\n     \\[\n     \\cos 45^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}a/2}{\\sqrt{h^2 + (3a^2)/4}}\n     \\]\n   - Solving this gives \\(h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}a}{2}\\).\n\n3. **Cross-Section Area Calculation**:\n   - The area \\(S\\) of the cross-section (triangle \\(ABC'\\)) is calculated using the cross product of vectors:\n     \\[\n     S = \\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{a^2 h^2 + \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}a^2}{2}\\right)^2}\n     \\]\n   - Substituting \\(h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}a}{2}\\) into the area formula, we get:\n     \\[\n     S = \\frac{\\sqrt{6}a^2}{4}\n     \\]\n   - Solving for \\(a^2\\) gives \\(a^2 = \\frac{4S}{\\sqrt{6}}\\).\n\n4. **Volume Calculation**:\n   - The volume \\(V\\) of the prism is given by the base area multiplied by the height:\n     \\[\n     V = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}a^2 \\cdot h\n     \\]\n   - Substituting \\(h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}a}{2}\\) and \\(a^2 = \\frac{4S}{\\sqrt{6}}\\) into the volume formula, we get:\n     \\[\n     V = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\cdot \\frac{4S}{\\sqrt{6}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}a}{2}\n     \\]\n   - Simplifying this expression, we find:\n     \\[\n     V = \\frac{3}{8}a^3\n     \\]\n   - Expressing \\(a^3\\) in terms of \\(S\\), we finally get:\n     \\[\n     V = \\frac{6^{1/4} \\cdot S^{3/2}}{2}\n     \\]\n\nThus, the volume of the prism is \\(\\boxed{\\dfrac{S^{3/2} \\sqrt[4]{6}}{2}}\\).", "ground_truth_solution": "\n1. To find the volume of the prism, we first analyze the triangular section that slices through the prism. Let the regular triangular prism be denoted by \\( A B C A_1 B_1 C_1 \\) and the cross-section plane is given as \\( \\triangle A C_1 B \\) which passes through the side \\( AB \\) of the lower base and the opposite vertex \\( C_1 \\) of the upper base (see 